e":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 10:07PM MDT until October 23 at 11:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache County in central Colorado...\nMineral County in south central Colorado...\nRio Grande County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Several structures are flooded and sand bagging\noperations are continuing. Evacuations are occuring from Wolf Creek\nRanch to Fun Valley. Some roads remain closed due to flooding\nincluding highway 160 and FR380.  The Park Creek bridge has been\nwashed away with considerable debris in the water.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1002 PM MDT, emergency management reported heavy rain in the\nwarned area. Flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\nBetween 1 and 3.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nThe Rio Grande River and its tributaries including the South Fork\narea and along highway 160 to Wolf Creek Pass.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T11:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO; Saguache, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.03011cf1c8199da5de650405af1eee2a145ac204.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 22 at 9:43PM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Through Friday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Ample sub-tropical moisture will bring periods of moderate to\nheavy rain across the area from tonight into Friday morning\nbefore winding down Friday afternoon.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07b206f85aa13647288ef4fe258fb417ba10c3ce.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.07b206f85aa13647288ef4fe258fb417ba10c3ce.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T11:23:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231123 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 523 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains in effect through this afternoon for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Rainfall starting to diminish across the higher terrain through this morning, then s","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T07:08:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 230708 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 108 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mosq","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T06:45:00+00:00","snippet":".Discussion... Critical fire weather conditions are NOT anticipated over the next 7 days. A Pacific storm system will bring widespread showers and thunderstorms, some strong, to the district today and